Package: eazy
Version: 5.2.0+rev45
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: eazy contributors <vapesmadcat-blip@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: bash, python3, fzf, whiptail, gawk, findutils, sed, coreutils, wget | curl
Recommends: mpv | mplayer | vlc, ffmpeg, yt-dlp, gcc
Suggests: aria2, axel, chafa, p7zip-full, rar, pciutils, alsa-utils, pulseaudio-utils, lshw, smartmontools, dmidecode, inxi, usbutils, x11-xserver-utils, mesa-utils, vulkan-tools, iw, network-manager, upower, lm-sensors
Description: terminal media browser and player
 eazy is a keyboard-driven terminal media browser and player built around
 fzf and a command-line media player. It provides persistent queues,
 recursive search, previews, playlists, downloads, and session state.
 .
 The package installs the application and command-line tools in /usr/bin,
 with supporting Python and C helpers in /usr/lib/eazy. It also includes
 a desktop launcher, a manual page, and current TXT and HTML help.
 User data is stored below ~/.config/eazy and is not removed on package removal.
